"The Aga's men took the pilgrims' money. Find little Luka and take them all home across the sea."
msgstr ""
"Die Männer des Agas haben das Geld der Pilger genommen. Findet den kleinen Luka und bringt alle "
"übers Meer heim."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The whole floor of Otranto cathedral is one huge mosaic, made in the 1160s by artists led by a "
"monk called Pantaleon, with a great Tree of Life running along it."
msgstr ""
"Der ganze Boden der Kathedrale von Otranto ist ein riesiges Mosaik. Künstler unter einem Mönch "
"namens Pantaleon schufen es um 1165, und ein großer Lebensbaum zieht sich hindurch."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The pilgrims are home!"
msgstr "Die Pilger sind zu Hause!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You found Luka and took the pilgrims home across the sea."
msgstr "Ihr habt Luka gefunden und die Pilger übers Meer heimgebracht."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "In Ragusa, the bells ring for them."
msgstr "In Ragusa läuten die Glocken für sie."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! The corsairs of Ulcinj took all our olive oil."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}! Die Korsaren von Ulcinj haben unser ganzes "
"Olivenöl genommen."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "We traded it for the winter, and now we have nothing."
msgstr "Es war unser Tauschgut für den Winter, und jetzt haben wir nichts."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Nobody fights them. Go and ask what they want for it!"
msgstr "Niemand kämpft gegen sie. Fragt, was sie dafür haben wollen!"

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oil for oil? No, no. My sail is torn to rags."
msgstr "Öl gegen Öl? Nein, nein. Mein Segel ist ganz zerfetzt."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me a new sail, and you get your oil back."
msgstr "Bringt mir ein neues Segel, dann bekommt ihr euer Öl zurück."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The sailmaker of Durrës makes the best sails."
msgstr "Der Segelmacher von Durrës macht die besten Segel."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A new sail! Fine work. Here is your oil, captain."
msgstr ""
"Ein neues Segel! Feine Arbeit. Hier ist euer Öl, {crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And tell the Aga that Crooked Mast is not his friend."
msgstr "Und sagt dem Aga, dass Schiefmast nicht sein Freund ist."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A sail? Gladly, but my cough is so bad, I can not work."
msgstr "Ein Segel? Gern, aber mein Husten ist so schlimm, ich kann nicht arbeiten."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Only the honey of Vlorë helps."
msgstr "Nur der Honig aus Vlorë hilft."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me a jar of honey!"
msgstr "Bringt mir einen Topf Honig!"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey from Vlorë! My cough is gone already."
msgstr "Honig aus Vlorë! Mein Husten ist schon weg."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the sail. The finest in the Adriatic!"
msgstr "Hier ist das Segel. Das schönste der ganzen Adria!"

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey? My bees made plenty."
msgstr "Honig? Davon haben meine Bienen reichlich gemacht."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But I need salt for my cheese. Do you have salt on board?"
msgstr "Aber ich brauche Salz für meinen Käse. Habt ihr Salz an Bord?"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt! Just what I needed."
msgstr "Salz! Genau das, was ich brauche."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is a jar of my best honey."
msgstr "Hier ist ein Topf von meinem besten Honig."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the olive oil home to {port}."
msgstr "Bringt das Olivenöl heim {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Our oil! Now we have enough for the winter."
msgstr "Unser Öl! Jetzt haben wir genug für den Winter."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast sent a message, too:"
msgstr "Schiefmast hat auch eine Nachricht geschickt:"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"The Aga's scribe sails south with a heavy book. Watch out for him!\""
msgstr "„Der Schreiber des Agas segelt mit einem dicken Buch nach Süden. Haltet Ausschau nach ihm!“"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Corsairs of Ulcinj"
msgstr "Die Korsaren von Ulcinj"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The corsairs took the villages' olive oil. Find out what they want, and trade it back."
msgstr ""
"Die Korsaren haben das Olivenöl der Dörfer genommen. Findet heraus, was sie wollen, und tauscht es"
" zurück."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The olive trees of the Adriatic grow very old: near Bar in Montenegro stands an olive tree which "
"is said to be more than two thousand years old."
msgstr ""
"Die Olivenbäume der Adria werden sehr alt: Bei Bar in Montenegro steht ein Olivenbaum, der mehr "
"als zweitausend Jahre alt sein soll."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oil is home!"
msgstr "Das Öl ist zu Hause!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Not a single shot was fired: a sail, a jar of honey and a sack of salt did it."
msgstr "Kein einziger Schuss fiel: Ein Segel, ein Topf Honig und ein Sack Salz haben es geschafft."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Even the corsair captain is your friend now."
msgstr "Sogar der Korsarenkapitän ist jetzt euer Freund."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Aga wants the oranges of Parga as a tax!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}, der Aga will die Orangen von Parga als Steuer!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eleni of Parga hid the harvest from his men."
msgstr "Eleni aus Parga hat die Ernte vor seinen Männern versteckt."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Help her get the oranges to the market of Corfu, so that the money stays with the people."
msgstr ""
"Helft ihr, die Orangen zum Markt von Korfu zu bringen, damit das Geld bei den Leuten bleibt."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oranges are ripe, but the Aga's men broke all my baskets."
msgstr "Die Orangen sind reif, aber die Männer des Agas haben alle meine Körbe kaputt gemacht."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me baskets! Ilir of Vlorë weaves the best ones."
msgstr "Bringt mir Körbe! Ilir aus Vlorë flicht die besten."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fine baskets! Here are the oranges, captain."
msgstr "Schöne Körbe! Hier sind die Orangen, {crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Smell them: the sun of Parga is inside."
msgstr "Riecht mal: Da steckt die Sonne von Parga drin."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I weave baskets from the reeds of the lagoon."
msgstr "Ich flechte Körbe aus dem Schilf der Lagune."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But my boat lost its rope. Spiros in Corfu has ropes!"
msgstr "Aber mein Boot hat sein Seil verloren. Spiros auf Korfu hat Seile!"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good rope! Here are my baskets."
msgstr "Ein gutes Seil! Hier sind meine Körbe."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A rope for Ilir? The harbour of Corfu has ropes for everybody."
msgstr "Ein Seil für Ilir? Der Hafen von Korfu hat Seile für alle."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take this one, captain."
msgstr "Nehmt dieses hier, {crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the oranges to the market of {port}."
msgstr "Bringt die Orangen zum Markt von {port}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oranges from Parga! The whole market smells of them."
msgstr "Orangen aus Parga! Der ganze Markt duftet danach."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The money goes to the people of Parga, not to the Aga."
msgstr "Das Geld geht an die Leute von Parga, nicht an den Aga."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every orange was sold, and Parga keeps its money."
msgstr "Jede Orange wurde verkauft, und Parga behält sein Geld."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga gets only the peels!"
msgstr "Der Aga bekommt nur die Schalen!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Oranges of Parga"
msgstr "Die Orangen von Parga"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Aga wants the oranges of Parga as a tax. Trade your way to baskets and bring the oranges to "
"the market of Corfu."
msgstr ""
"Der Aga will die Orangen von Parga als Steuer. Tauscht euch bis zu den Körben durch und bringt die"
" Orangen zum Markt von Korfu."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Parga was a little Venetian town on the Greek coast for almost 400 years, with Ottoman lands all "
"around it, and it was often raided by its neighbours."
msgstr ""
"Parga war fast 400 Jahre lang ein kleines venezianisches Städtchen an der griechischen Küste, "
"rundherum osmanisches Land, und die Nachbarn überfielen es oft."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sweet oranges for Corfu!"
msgstr "Süße Orangen für Korfu!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oranges reached the market, and the money stayed in Parga."
msgstr "Die Orangen kamen auf den Markt, und das Geld blieb in Parga."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A rope, a basket and a lot of sailing did it."
msgstr "Ein Seil, ein Korb und viel Segeln haben es geschafft."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the warning of Crooked Mast came true!"
msgstr "{crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}, die Warnung von Schiefmast war richtig!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's scribe was here with a heavy book: the ledger of the double taxes."
msgstr "Der Schreiber des Agas war hier, mit einem dicken Buch: dem Buch der doppelten Steuern."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "With it, we can prove everything. But he fled in a hurry. Chase him!"
msgstr "Damit können wir alles beweisen. Aber er ist in Eile geflohen. Jagt ihm nach!"

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The scribe had {hallmark}."
msgstr "Der Schreiber hatte {hallmark@acc}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the Aga's scribe with a heavy book?"
msgstr "Habt ihr den Schreiber des Agas mit einem dicken Buch gesehen?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres data/missions/24_count_flees/mission.tres
#: data/missions/32_stewards_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He is here, hiding among the people of the harbour! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Er ist hier und versteckt sich unter den Leuten im Hafen! Aber welcher ist er?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is the Aga's scribe?"
msgstr "Welcher ist der Schreiber des Agas?"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not the scribe! Remember all four things you learned."
msgstr "Nein, das ist nicht der Schreiber! Denkt an alle vier Dinge, die ihr erfahren habt."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Alright, alright! Here is the ledger. I only wrote what the Aga told me!\""
msgstr ""
"„Schon gut, schon gut! Hier ist das Steuerbuch. Ich habe nur geschrieben, was der Aga mir gesagt "
"hat!“"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"I will tell the truth before the judge, I promise.\""
msgstr "„Ich sage vor dem Richter die Wahrheit, versprochen.“"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ledger proves it: the Aga took every tax twice!"
msgstr "Das Steuerbuch beweist es: Der Aga hat jede Steuer doppelt kassiert!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Forged Ledger"
msgstr "Das gefälschte Steuerbuch"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's scribe flees with the ledger of the double taxes. Chase him along the coast!"
msgstr ""
"Der Schreiber des Agas flieht mit dem Buch der doppelten Steuern. Jagt ihn die Küste entlang!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Spectacles were made in Venice from about 1300 on; the glassmakers of Murano were so precious that"
" they were not allowed to leave the republic."
msgstr ""
"Brillen wurden in Venedig ab etwa 1300 gemacht. Die Glasmacher von Murano waren so wertvoll, dass "
"sie die Republik nicht verlassen durften."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ledger is yours!"
msgstr "Das Steuerbuch gehört euch!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You chased the scribe along the whole coast and found him."
msgstr "Ihr habt den Schreiber die ganze Küste entlang gejagt und gefunden."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the crew holds the proof of the double taxes."
msgstr "Jetzt hat die Mannschaft den Beweis für die doppelten Steuern."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, I must confess something."
msgstr "{crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}, ich muss etwas gestehen."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I wrote the list of the villages in the old Glagolitic letters, so that the Aga could not read it."
msgstr ""
"Ich habe die Liste der Dörfer in den alten glagolitischen Buchstaben geschrieben, damit der Aga "
"sie nicht lesen kann."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now I can not read it either! Find a priest who knows the old letters."
msgstr "Jetzt kann ich sie auch nicht lesen! Findet einen Priester, der die alten Buchstaben kennt."

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The priest has {hallmark}."
msgstr "Der Priester hat {hallmark@acc}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen a priest who knows the old letters?"
msgstr "Habt ihr einen Priester gesehen, der die alten Buchstaben kennt?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Don Grgur is here, at the market! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Don Grgur ist hier, auf dem Markt! Aber welcher ist er?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is Don Grgur? Remember what the people told you!"
msgstr "Welcher ist Don Grgur? Denkt daran, was die Leute euch erzählt haben!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not him! Think of all three things you learned."
msgstr "Nein, das ist er nicht! Denkt an alle drei Dinge, die ihr erfahren habt."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Yes, I read the old letters. Let me see... every village, and every ducat!\""
msgstr "„Ja, ich lese die alten Buchstaben. Mal sehen... jedes Dorf und jeder Dukat!“"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the list back to the scribe in {port}."
msgstr "Bringt die Liste zurück zum Schreiber {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every village and every ducat, written clearly at last!"
msgstr "Jedes Dorf und jeder Dukat, endlich klar geschrieben!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the judge can give back every coin."
msgstr "Jetzt kann der Richter jede Münze zurückgeben."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The list is ready for the judge."
msgstr "Die Liste ist bereit für den Richter."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will never write in a secret script again!"
msgstr "Ich schreibe nie wieder in einer Geheimschrift!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Secret Script"
msgstr "Die Geheimschrift"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The list of the villages is written in old Glagolitic letters. Find a priest who can read it."
msgstr ""
"Die Liste der Dörfer ist in alten glagolitischen Buchstaben geschrieben. Findet einen Priester, "
"der sie lesen kann."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Glagolitic is the oldest known Slavic alphabet. On the islands of Kvarner, like Krk, and on the "
"islands near Zadar, Croatian priests and scribes kept writing in it for centuries."
msgstr ""
"Die Glagoliza ist das älteste bekannte slawische Alphabet. Auf den Kvarner-Inseln wie Krk und auf "
"den Inseln bei Zadar schrieben kroatische Priester und Schreiber noch Jahrhunderte lang damit."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The list is read!"
msgstr "Die Liste ist gelesen!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Don Grgur read the old letters for you."
msgstr "Don Grgur hat die alten Buchstaben für euch gelesen."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the judge will know every village and every ducat."
msgstr "Jetzt kennt der Richter jedes Dorf und jeden Dukaten."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the judge wants to hear witnesses, not only the ledger."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}, der Richter will Zeugen hören, nicht nur das "
"Steuerbuch."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast in Ulcinj, Mustafa in Castelnuovo and Jele in Kotor saw what the Aga's men did."
msgstr ""
"Schiefmast in Ulcinj, Mustafa in Castelnuovo und Jele in Kotor haben gesehen, was die Männer des "
"Agas getan haben."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring all three to Corfu, where the voyage to the judge begins!"
msgstr "Bringt alle drei nach Korfu, wo die Reise zum Richter beginnt!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Me, a witness? Ha! Fine."
msgstr "Ich, ein Zeuge? Ha! Na gut."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I saw the Aga's men take a tax twice, right at sea."
msgstr ""
"Ich habe gesehen, wie die Männer des Agas eine Steuer doppelt kassiert haben, mitten auf See."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I keep the gate of Castelnuovo."
msgstr "Ich bewache das Tor von Castelnuovo."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every cart of the Aga's men went through it, twice."
msgstr "Jeder Karren der Männer des Agas fuhr hindurch, zweimal."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "They took my olives as a tax, and came back a week later for more."
msgstr ""
"Sie haben meine Oliven als Steuer genommen und kamen eine Woche später wieder, um mehr zu holen."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judge everything."
msgstr "Ich erzähle dem Richter alles."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#: data/missions/25_royal_audience_of_trani/mission.tres
#: data/missions/34_through_the_bura/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pick up {count} more {count|witness|witnesses}."
msgstr "Holt noch {count} {count|Zeugen|Zeugen} ab."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the witnesses to {port}."
msgstr "Bringt die Zeugen {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast? A corsair as a witness... the judge will be surprised!"
msgstr "Schiefmast? Ein Korsar als Zeuge... der Richter wird staunen!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Mustafa, the gatekeeper. Welcome to Corfu!"
msgstr "Mustafa, der Torwächter. Willkommen auf Korfu!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Jele of Kotor. Rest a little, the voyage is long."
msgstr "Jele aus Kotor. Ruh dich ein wenig aus, die Reise ist lang."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The witnesses are ready, and so is the ledger."
msgstr "Die Zeugen sind bereit, und das Steuerbuch auch."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Soon, the voyage to the judge begins!"
msgstr "Bald beginnt die Reise zum Richter!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Witnesses"
msgstr "Die Zeugen"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The judge wants to hear witnesses. Bring them from Ulcinj, Castelnuovo and Kotor to Corfu."
msgstr "Der Richter will Zeugen hören. Bringt sie aus Ulcinj, Castelnuovo und Kotor nach Korfu."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Republic of Ragusa banned the slave trade in 1416. It valued freedom very highly: the word "
"Libertas stands on its flag."
msgstr ""
"Die Republik Ragusa verbot 1416 den Sklavenhandel. Die Freiheit war ihr sehr wichtig: Auf ihrer "
"Flagge steht das Wort Libertas."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The witnesses are ready!"
msgstr "Die Zeugen sind bereit!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A corsair, a gatekeeper and an olive grower will speak before the judge."
msgstr "Ein Korsar, ein Torwächter und eine Olivenbäuerin sprechen vor dem Richter."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's days as a tax collector are numbered."
msgstr "Die Tage des Agas als Steuereintreiber sind gezählt."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the day has come!"
msgstr "{crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}, der Tag ist gekommen!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the ledger and the witnesses to the kadı of Preveza: he judges by the law."
msgstr "Bringt das Steuerbuch und die Zeugen zum Kadi von Preveza: Er urteilt nach dem Gesetz."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Master Ivan waits in Parga, and Doctor Marin is here in Corfu."
msgstr "Meister Ivan wartet in Parga, und Doktor Marin ist hier auf Korfu."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I am ready, captain. I will tell the judge about the fever."
msgstr ""
"Ich bin bereit, {crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}. Ich erzähle dem Richter vom "
"Fieber."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! I came all the way from Pula."
msgstr "{crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}! Ich bin den weiten Weg aus Pula gekommen."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judge about the Aga's recruiter."
msgstr "Ich erzähle dem Richter vom Werber des Agas."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the ledger and the witnesses to {port}."
msgstr "Bringt das Steuerbuch und die Zeugen {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Peace be with you. Show me the ledger, and let the witnesses speak."
msgstr "Friede sei mit euch. Zeigt mir das Steuerbuch, und lasst die Zeugen sprechen."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which village lost its bell?"
msgstr "Welches Dorf hat seine Glocke verloren?"

