#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Welcome to Loreto, pilgrims!"
msgstr "Willkommen in Loreto, liebe Pilger!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And not a single coin for the Count's toll."
msgstr "Und keine einzige Münze für den Zoll des Grafen."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The pilgrims pray in the Holy House, and they sing all the way home."
msgstr "Die Pilger beten im Heiligen Haus und singen auf dem ganzen Heimweg."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And the Count's toll man? He went home to think about riddles."
msgstr "Und der Zöllner des Grafen? Der ist heimgegangen, um über Rätsel nachzudenken."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Pilgrims of Loreto"
msgstr "Die Pilger von Loreto"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Carry the pilgrims of Pescara past the Count's \"pilgrim toll\" to the Holy House of Loreto."
msgstr ""
"Bringt die Pilger aus Pescara am „Pilgerzoll“ des Grafen vorbei zum Heiligen Haus von Loreto."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A legend says that angels carried the Holy House of Mary from Nazareth to Loreto. Because of that "
"flying house, the Madonna of Loreto became the patron saint of pilots in 1920."
msgstr ""
"Eine Legende sagt, Engel hätten das Heilige Haus Marias von Nazareth nach Loreto getragen. Wegen "
"dieses fliegenden Hauses wurde die Madonna von Loreto 1920 die Schutzpatronin der Flieger."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The pilgrims reached Loreto!"
msgstr "Die Pilger sind in Loreto!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You carried the pilgrims past the Count's toll."
msgstr "Ihr habt die Pilger am Zoll des Grafen vorbeigebracht."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/18_pilgrims_of_loreto/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Not one of them paid a coin."
msgstr "Keiner von ihnen hat eine Münze bezahlt."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count's toll man left behind a page of the Count's charter."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}, der Zöllner des Grafen hat eine Seite der Urkunde "
"des Grafen verloren."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count says it is twenty years old. A paper merchant could tell!"
msgstr "Der Graf sagt, sie ist zwanzig Jahre alt. Ein Papierhändler könnte das prüfen!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ser Anselmo of Fabriano sails along the coast. Find him!"
msgstr "Ser Anselmo aus Fabriano segelt die Küste entlang. Findet ihn!"

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The paper merchant has {hallmark}."
msgstr "Der Papierhändler hat {hallmark@acc}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen Ser Anselmo, the paper merchant?"
msgstr "Habt ihr Ser Anselmo gesehen, den Papierhändler?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He is here, at the market! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Er ist hier, auf dem Markt! Aber welcher ist er?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is Ser Anselmo? Remember what the people told you!"
msgstr "Welcher ist Ser Anselmo? Denkt daran, was die Leute euch erzählt haben!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not Ser Anselmo! Think of everything you heard."
msgstr "Nein, das ist nicht Ser Anselmo! Denkt an alles, was ihr gehört habt."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"A paper with a secret? Take me to it, captain!\""
msgstr "„Ein Papier mit einem Geheimnis? Bringt mich hin!“"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring Ser Anselmo to {port}."
msgstr "Bringt Ser Anselmo {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ser Anselmo holds the page against the light."
msgstr "Ser Anselmo hält die Seite gegen das Licht."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"See the watermark? This paper was made in Fabriano only this year!\""
msgstr "„Seht ihr das Wasserzeichen? Dieses Papier wurde erst dieses Jahr in Fabriano gemacht!“"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "So it can not be twenty years old. That is our first proof!"
msgstr "Also kann es nicht zwanzig Jahre alt sein. Das ist unser erster Beweis!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A watermark never lies, captain."
msgstr "Ein Wasserzeichen lügt nie, {crew|Kapitän|Kapitänin|Kapitäne|Kapitäninnen}."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count can forge words, but not the paper of Fabriano!"
msgstr "Der Graf kann Worte fälschen, aber nicht das Papier von Fabriano!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Paper with a Secret"
msgstr "Das Papier mit dem Geheimnis"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Find the paper merchant who can read the charter against the light. Proof 1: the watermark of "
"Fabriano."
msgstr ""
"Findet den Papierhändler, der die Urkunde gegen das Licht lesen kann. Beweis 1: das Wasserzeichen "
"von Fabriano."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The paper mills of Fabriano were among the first in Europe. Their papermakers invented the "
"watermark: a picture inside the paper, which shows only against the light."
msgstr ""
"Die Papiermühlen von Fabriano gehörten zu den ersten in Europa. Ihre Papiermacher erfanden das "
"Wasserzeichen: ein Bild im Papier, das man nur gegen das Licht sieht."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The first proof!"
msgstr "Der erste Beweis!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You found Ser Anselmo, and the watermark speaks."
msgstr "Ihr habt Ser Anselmo gefunden, und das Wasserzeichen spricht."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/19_paper_with_a_secret/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Count's paper is new, not twenty years old."
msgstr "Das Papier des Grafen ist neu, nicht zwanzig Jahre alt."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/20_seal_maker_of_ortona/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Count's seal looks like the seal of the Viceroy."
